UDDI :
------

UDDI stands for Universal Description, Discovery, and Integration.
It is basically a directory service for web services, like a “yellow pages”
where businesses can publish and find web services on the internet or within an enterprise.

Key Points about UDDI
---------------------
Universal Description – Stores information about web services (like service name, provider, and usage details).
Discovery – Allows clients or systems to search for services based on specific criteria.
Integration – Provides the technical information (like WSDL URL) required to integrate with that service.

UDDI in Web Services
---------------------
Works together with SOAP and WSDL:
WSDL describes how to call the service.
SOAP is the protocol for communication.
UDDI tells you where to find the service.

Simple Example
---------------
A company develops a Currency Conversion Web Service.
They publish it in the UDDI Registry with details like:
Service Name: CurrencyConversionService
WSDL URL: http://example.com/CurrencyConversion?wsdl
Another company searches the UDDI Registry, finds this service, and integrates it into their application.